    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 1 needs assessment and gap analysis in relation to IAT, SALW control, possession and misuse and weapons categorization prepared per jurisdiction
2. At least 4 institutional capacity trainings delivered, with a total of 60 police officers from each jurisdiction trained (including trainings on information gathering, information sharing and information analysis and number of trainings on weapons 
categorization)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Needs assessment and gap analysis in relation to IAT, SALW control, possession and misuse and weapons categorization completed and presented to project beneficiary at a dedicated workshop. This needs assessment and gap analysis is focused on identifying the main gaps in relation to IAT, SALW control, possession and misuse and weapons categorization in the project beneficiary, and to provide solutions.

2. Completed 6 institutional capacity trainings, 4 in Skopje (trainings on information gathering, information sharing and information analysis) and 2 trainings on weapons categorization in Prishtina, for a total of 60 police officers from both jusidctions. The training programme and curriculum were based on the needs assessment and gap analysis and serve to fulfill the identified gaps in the project beneficiary. The trainings will continue in 2022, in order to increase the capacities of an even larger number of police officers in the Ministry of Interior.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Trained a total of 280 police officers from both jurisidctionsin information gathering, information sharing and information analysis, and a total of 340 police officers in weapons catgorisation. 
2. Prepared training materials on converted-firearms investigations and completed 3 trainings on establishing trafficking routes, integrated use of financial investigation during IAT cases and firearms-conversion methods and table-top exercises.
3. Prepared knowledge products/SOP on converted firearms investigations.
4. Developed knowledge products/SOP on cyber crime related to illicit arms trafficking.
5. Improved public awareness through 2 mass-media campaigns, 4 targeted campaigns in communities and a visibility event.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
